title: nemesis2_defense
---
Narrator:
You are inside the perimeter now.

---

Narrator:
The systems here feel different. Not defended by fleets, exactly — but watched. Every approach is observed. Every course correction logged.

Your security officer has stopped counting the passive sensors. There are too many.

---

Narrator:
The first resistance is not military.

A broadcast, system-wide, in six languages. One of them is yours.

It says: You have entered sovereign space. State your purpose.

---

Narrator:
Your tactical officer notes that there are three firing solutions painted on your lead vessel. All within range. None have fired.

---

-> [Broadcast your purpose — claim right of passage]
    <<apply_effect "inner_sanctum_key">>
    Narrator:
    You broadcast in all six languages.

    Narrator:
    There is a pause. Long enough to be meaningful. Short enough to be calculated.

    Narrator:
    The firing solutions drop. A single vessel, sleek and marked, escorts you to the system edge.

    Narrator:
    Your security officer says: they respected the protocol. Whatever they are, they operate by rules.

    Narrator:
    That is either reassuring or terrifying. She can't decide which.

-> [Say nothing — continue the advance]
    <<apply_effect "nemesis_curse">>
    <<chain_event "nemesis2_sanctum">>
    Narrator:
    You don't respond. The fleet advances.

    Narrator:
    The firing solutions hold.

    Narrator:
    Then one of them fires.

    Narrator:
    A warning shot. Precisely calculated to miss by exactly ten metres.

    Narrator:
    Your tactical officer says: they could have killed us. They chose not to.

    Narrator:
    You don't know if that makes things better or worse.

===
